# PK:
# Passive LC EQ — Pultec EQP-1A-inspired passive program equalizer. Boost and
# cut shaped by RC shelves and a series-resonant LC high boost that never
# sounds harsh.
# Type: equalizer (outboard studio gear)
#
# PROVENANCE — Pultec EQP-1A (Pulse Techniques, ~1961)
#   Architecture: an entirely PASSIVE equalizer section — bridged-T-ish RC
#   shelving for the low band, a series-resonant LC section for the high
#   boost, an RC shelf for the high cut — followed by a tube makeup amplifier
#   that recovers the network's flat insertion loss (~16 dB in the real
#   unit). Because boost and cut networks are separate, engaging LF boost and
#   LF cut TOGETHER produces the famous shelf-plus-dip "Pultec trick".
#   Real makeup amp: push-pull 12AX7 -> 12AU7 with transformer feedback.
#
# KEY FREQUENCIES (real unit):
#   LF boost/cut: 20 / 30 / 60 / 100 Hz (switched caps, RC — NO inductor in
#                 the low band of the real EQP-1A)
#   HF boost:     3 / 4 / 5 / 8 / 10 / 12 / 16 kHz — switched inductor taps;
#                 measured tap values are on the order of
#                 27m / 33m / 47m / 68m / 82m / 150m henries
#   HF cut (atten): 5 / 10 / 20 kHz RC shelf
#
# AS MODELED HERE (four cascaded passive sections + 12AX7 makeup,
# verified responsive — sweeps in tests/pultec_sweeps.rs):
#   0. LF CUT shelf: LF_Cut pot (10k) in the series arm, bypassed at HF by
#      C_lcut (47n, via R_lcsep — see note 3). At LF the cap blocks and the
#      pot's resistance pads the signal -> shelf cut. Corner at full
#      rotation ~ 1/(2*pi * 10k * 47n) ~= 339 Hz, sliding up as depth rises.
#   1. LF BOOST shelf: R1 (10k series) into a shunt leg of R_s1 (2.7k) in
#      series with (C_lf || LF_Boost pot). At low frequencies the cap blocks,
#      the pot raises the shunt impedance -> less attenuation -> shelf boost.
#      Corner f = 1/(2*pi * 10k * C_lf): 270n -> ~59 Hz (the "60 CPS" panel
#      position).
#   2. HF BOOST: series-resonant L+C branch bypasses series resistor R2 at
#      resonance. C_hf chosen so 47 mH resonates near 5 kHz:
#      C = 1/(L*(2*pi*f)^2) = 1/(0.047*(2*pi*5000)^2) ~= 21.6n -> 22n
#      (f0 = 1/(2*pi*sqrt(0.047 * 22n)) ~= 4.95 kHz).
#      HF_Boost pot = series damping (boost amount), HF_BW pot = additional
#      series damping in the resonant branch (bandwidth/Q).
#   3. HF CUT: HF_Atten pot + 6.8n cap shunt to ground after separation
#      resistor R3.
#   4. MAKEUP: single 12AX7 common-cathode stage (100k plate / bypassed 1.5k
#      cathode, B+ 250V), AC-coupled after the network. Recovers the passive
#      pad's ~-29 dB; net chain gain ~+4.3 dB at 1 kHz.
#
# SIMPLIFICATIONS vs real unit (audit notes — deviations are intentional):
#   1. MAKEUP STAGE (updated 2026-06-12): with the F10 passive-claiming fix,
#      an AC-coupled triode makeup AFTER the network no longer flattens the
#      passives or freezes the pots (pattern from tests/passive_claiming.rs).
#      v1's finding — every makeup attempt silenced the EQ or froze the
#      controls — is obsolete. The makeup here is a single 12AX7 stage, not
#      the real push-pull 12AX7 -> 12AU7 with transformer feedback.
#   2. NO SWITCHED COMPONENTS — with the F7 fix, cap_switched /
#      inductor_switched compile in passive trees but the switch is frozen
#      at position 0, which would pin the EQ to the first tap (150n / 27m =
#      the 106 Hz / 6.5 kHz positions). Fixed values are kept instead:
#      C_lf = 270n (60 Hz position), L_hf = 47m + 22n (~5 kHz position).
#      Re-introduce switched values once positions are runtime-selectable.
#   3. SEPARATION RESISTORS are engine workarounds, not in the real unit:
#      - R3 (4.7k): three branch sections sharing one node collapse to a
#        passthrough without it (verified: all deltas +0.00 dB).
#      - R_lcsep (100R): NEW finding (2026-06-12) — wiring LF_Cut and C_lcut
#        as exact parallel edges between the same two nodes collapses the
#        WHOLE network to silence (every probe < -157 dB). Breaking the
#        exact parallel with a 100R resistor in the cap branch restores
#        normal compilation.
#   4. HF boost amount is a series damping pot inside the LC branch, not the
#      real pot-across-the-tank arrangement. The Bandwidth pot is ALSO series
#      damping (a pot in parallel with the inductor — the more physical
#      damping arrangement — is another collapse trigger: with HF_BW across
#      L_hf the entire network compiled to a passthrough). Boost and
#      Bandwidth therefore interact much more strongly than in the real unit.
#      ENGINE GAP (2026-06-12): the L+C reactance of the pot-bearing branch
#      is mostly lost in compilation — divider math predicts a ~+13.6 dB
#      resonant peak at 4.95 kHz with minimum damping, but the measured
#      boost is a broad +1.4 dB hump. Its maximum DOES sit at ~5-7 kHz
#      (within an octave of f0), so the peak location is honest even though
#      the peak height is ~12 dB short.
#   5. LF cut section ADDED 2026-06-12 (was omitted in v1) — the "Pultec
#      trick" (simultaneous LF boost+cut) now measures: LF Boost 0.7 +
#      LF Cut 0.7 vs flat shows +0.5..+0.8 dB lift below 100 Hz and a
#      -0.4..-0.55 dB dip at 200-630 Hz (centered ~350 Hz). Depths are
#      ~5-10x smaller than the real unit's because pot authority through
#      the compiled passive tree is weak (boost full-throw ~+3.6 dB).
#   6. NO input/output transformers (real: 600 ohm bridging iron both ends).
#   7. Response artifact: the compiled chain rolls off steeply above
#      ~12 kHz (-32 dB at 15 kHz, < -100 dB at 20 kHz) regardless of control
#      settings — engine artifact, present in the passive-only version too.
#      Sweep assertions stay at or below ~11 kHz.
#   8. ENGINE GAP (2026-06-12, control sweeps): runtime set_control pot
#      POSITIONS BELOW 0.5 are aliased and non-physical in this compiled
#      passive tree — position 0.5 measures IDENTICAL to position 0.0, and
#      positions ~0.1-0.25 land outside the physically reachable range
#      (LF Boost 0.1 -> 2.8 dB BELOW the 1-ohm-pot floor; LF Cut 0.1 ->
#      2.1 dB ABOVE the flat response; both linear and audio tapers
#      affected). Compiled-in `controls { ... = X }` defaults are inert
#      (response always matches position 0 regardless of X). The upper half
#      of pot travel behaves physically and monotonically — sweeps in
#      tests/pultec_sweeps.rs assert on that window and carry #[ignore]'d
#      full-range red tests.
#
# Measured (48 kHz, 0.1 amplitude probes, this exact netlist, HF_BW = 0.5,
# full tables in reports/outboard-sweeps-2026-06-12.md):
#   Flat (all knobs 0):         +5.9 dB at 63 Hz, +4.3 dB at 1 kHz
#   LF Boost 0 -> 1 at 63 Hz:   +2.8 dB   (movement at 1 kHz: -0.2 dB)
#   LF Cut   0 -> 1 at 63 Hz:   -2.0 dB
#   HF Boost 0 -> 1 (BW 0):     +1.4 dB broad hump, max ~5-7 kHz
#   HF Atten 0 -> 1 at 8.4 kHz: -2.6 dB

equipment "Passive LC EQ EQP-1A" {
  supplies {
    B+: 250V               # Plate supply for the 12AX7 makeup stage
  }

  components {
    # === Input coupling ===
    C_in: cap(1u)

    # === Section 0: LF cut (attenuate) — series R||C shelf ===
    LF_Cut: pot(10k)          # 0 ohm = flat, 10k = max LF cut
    C_lcut: cap(47n)          # HF bypass around the cut pot
    R_lcsep: resistor(100)    # Separation resistor (breaks exact parallel edges)

    # === Section 1: LF boost shelf (RC — real EQP-1A low band is RC) ===
    R1: resistor(10k)         # Series arm
    R_s1: resistor(2.7k)      # Upper shunt arm
    C_lf: cap(270n)           # 60 Hz position (see audit note 2 — fixed value)
    LF_Boost: pot(10k, a)     # 10k boost pot — 0 ohm = flat, 10k = max shelf

    # === Section 2: HF boost — series-resonant LC bypass across R2 ===
    R2: resistor(10k)         # Series arm being bypassed at resonance
    HF_Boost: pot(100k, a)    # Series damping — boost amount (0 ohm = max,
                              # 100k = branch effectively out of circuit)
    L_hf: inductor(47m)       # EQP-1A measured tap value (5 kHz position)
    C_hf: cap(22n)            # Resonates 47m at ~4.95 kHz (see header math)
    HF_BW: pot(25k)           # Series damping in the branch — bandwidth/Q
                              # (see audit note 4: parallel-with-L collapses)
    R_s2: resistor(2.7k)      # Shunt arm of the section divider

    # === Section 3: HF cut (attenuate) shelf ===
    R3: resistor(4.7k)        # Separation resistor (engine workaround, note 3)
    HF_Atten: pot(50k, a)     # 0 ohm = max cut
    C_hcut: cap(6.8n)         # HF cut shunt cap

    # === Network load ===
    R_load: resistor(100k)    # Passive network load ahead of the makeup grid

    # === 12AX7 makeup gain stage (AC-coupled, passive_claiming.rs pattern) ===
    C_c: cap(22n)             # Coupling into the makeup grid
    R_g: resistor(1M)         # Grid leak
    V1: triode(12ax7)
    R_p: resistor(100k)       # Plate load
    R_k: resistor(1.5k)       # Cathode bias
    C_k: cap(25u, electrolytic) # Cathode bypass — full gain
    C_out: cap(22n)           # Output coupling
    R_out: resistor(1M)       # Output load
  }

  nets {
    # --- Input through the LF cut shelf into section 1 ---
    in -> C_in.a
    C_in.b -> LF_Cut.a, C_lcut.a
    C_lcut.b -> R_lcsep.a
    R_lcsep.b -> R1.a
    LF_Cut.b -> R1.a

    # --- Section 1: LF boost shelf ---
    # Shunt leg: R_s1 in series with (C_lf || LF_Boost) to ground. At LF the
    # cap blocks, so the pot raises the shunt impedance -> shelf boost.
    R1.b -> R_s1.a, R2.a
    R_s1.b -> C_lf.a, LF_Boost.a
    C_lf.b -> gnd
    LF_Boost.b -> gnd

    # --- Section 2: HF boost LC bypass across R2 ---
    R1.b -> HF_Boost.a
    HF_Boost.b -> L_hf.a
    L_hf.b -> C_hf.a
    C_hf.b -> HF_BW.a

    # Bandwidth: additional series damping lowers Q / softens the peak
    HF_BW.b -> R2.b

    # Section 2 divider shunt
    R2.b -> R_s2.a, R3.a
    R_s2.b -> gnd

    # --- Section 3: HF cut after the separation resistor ---
    R3.b -> HF_Atten.a, R_load.a, C_c.a
    HF_Atten.b -> C_hcut.a
    C_hcut.b -> gnd
    R_load.b -> gnd

    # --- 12AX7 makeup stage: 100k plate to B+, bypassed 1.5k cathode ---
    C_c.b -> R_g.a, V1.grid
    R_g.b -> gnd
    B+ -> R_p.a
    R_p.b -> V1.plate
    V1.cathode -> R_k.a, C_k.a
    R_k.b -> gnd
    C_k.b -> gnd
    V1.plate -> C_out.a
    C_out.b -> R_out.a, out
    R_out.b -> gnd
  }

  controls {
    # Ranges oriented so turning each knob UP gives MORE boost / MORE cut.
    LF_Boost.position -> "LF Boost" [0.0, 1.0] = 0.0
    LF_Cut.position -> "LF Cut" [0.0, 1.0] = 0.0
    HF_Boost.position -> "HF Boost" [1.0, 0.0] = 0.0
    HF_BW.position -> "HF Bandwidth" [0.0, 1.0] = 0.5
    HF_Atten.position -> "HF Atten" [1.0, 0.0] = 0.0
  }
}
